{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1517871-songs-for-the-dead-mtaw2e-ooc","id":1517871,"title":"Songs for the Dead [MTAW2E OOC]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play","Play by Post"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-13T06:18:27-07:00","id":1517871,"title":"Songs for the Dead [MTAW2E OOC]","content":"<br /> <br /> <b>Songs for the Dead</b><br /> <br /> <b>A Mage:The Awakening 2E Chronicle</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>\u201cBut where shall chochmah be found? And where is the makom binah? Enosh knoweth not the price thereof; neither is it found in the Eretz HaChayyim.The tehom saith, It is not in me; and the yam saith, It is not with me\u2026<br /> <br /> From where then cometh chochmah? And where is the makom binah? Seeing it is hidden from the eyes of kol chai, and concealed from the oph HaShomayim.<br /> <br /> Abaddon and Mavet say, \u2018We have heard a rumor thereof with our ears.\u201d</i><ul><li>Ancient Hebrew Text</li> </ul><br /> <br /> The Lie is that there is nothing after death. The Lie is that Death is an undiscovered country from whence travelers never return.<br /> <br /> <br /> This chronicle of Mage: The Awakening will follow a cabal of wisdom seekers through the many winding paths that lie under the shadow of Death.<br /> <br /> <br /> In celebration of the release of the newest 2E Mage book Tome of the Pentacle, the story will follow the player characters as they journey all around the world. They will explore many different cultures of magic through the one thing that unites all of humanity, asleep and awake, which is mortality. Everyone dies.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Theme is\u2026well\u2026Death. But also about the stories and songs that we tell ourselves about death, and maybe that the dead tell and sing also. As one writer put it, \u201cThe past is never dead. It\u2019s not even past.\u201d The characters will be exploring ancient mysteries and maybe even future events through their journey into the Great Below.<br /> <br /> <br /> We understand that in real life, many different people have many different experiences with and understandings of what death is. We want to be respectful of these viewpoints while exploring the topic through storytelling.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Mood is \u201cGlobetrotting Adventure\u201d. The characters will visit many different locations throughout the world and encounter the awakened, sleepers, and various supernatural characters while they travel. Yes, there will be cut scenes of airplanes, trains, and ships following red lines across maps (at least in the players\u2019 and readers\u2019 imaginations). There will be combat. And chases. And braving of the elements. And lots and lots of graveyards, catacombs, and tombs.<br /> <br /> <br /> This will be a tier 3 chronicle, with all that that implies. Rather than focusing on an isolated cabal, single consilium, or regional caucus, the player characters will be meddling in the affairs of the Pentacle Orders, and Seers of the Throne, as well as nameless orders, on a world-wide scale. They will probably make powerful enemies, and hopefully equally powerful friends.<br /> <br /> <br /> For some this will not just be an adventure though. It might become a pilgrimage. A race against evil perhaps. Or a quest for illumination.<br /> <br /> <br /> Again, we want to be respectful of all the real world locations, peoples, ethnicities, and cultures that will be represented. We want to celebrate the diversity and dignity of all of humanity through storytelling.<br /> <br /> This game is not currently recruiting.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T06:21:28-07:00","id":1517872,"title":"","content":"I was thinking we would probably start with Prologues, describing your character's most recent encounter with death, and then proceed to Buenos Aires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T07:02:24-07:00","id":1517874,"title":"","content":"I'll probably be saying this throughout the chronicle. This is a work of fictional storytelling. Upmost respect to the real world community of Tristan da Cunha and their cemetery. <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.tristandc.com/cemeteries.php\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.tristandc.com/images/hmsrcemview.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.tristandc.com/cemeteries.php\" target=\"_blank\"> Guide to the Tristan da Cunha Cemeteries </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.tristandc.com/cemeteries.php\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.tristandc.com/cemeteries.php </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Tristan da Cunha has three cemetaries, covering different periods in the island's history. There has been much restoration of graves during the new millennium. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T07:04:45-07:00","id":1517875,"title":"","content":"Oh. You can also put any brief introduction to your character that you would like to make here in this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T13:09:30-07:00","id":1517897,"title":"","content":"I created a document in the players folder with some information about Buenos Aires","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T23:50:23-07:00","id":1517922,"title":"","content":"Oh shoot, didn\u2019t see this. Sorry. Uh maybe we should summon the others, just in case they missed if. Hey, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28046-maroon_mumba\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar28046_1.webp');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28046\" data-vbnamecard=\"28046\">Maroon_Mumba</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28057-nickeldan\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28057\" data-vbnamecard=\"28057\">nickeldan</a>, we are live!<br /> <br /> Should we do the prologue first? Or the character introductions first? For the prologue, I was thinking this would be Katab received the summons to Buenos Aires. I was thinking it could happen while preparing go explore the Ossuary for the first time after getting access\u2026or it could be them paying off one of their ghostly contacts. Either way, they get a message from a person they respect\u2026basically anyone on the character sheet Calvin has made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T06:55:34-07:00","id":1517936,"title":"","content":"Spoiler for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26736_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26736\" data-vbnamecard=\"26736\">TempleBuilder</a> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> The grimoire castoff that Katab acquired for the Mysterium was based on a mundane text, written by a Dominican friar in the 16th century. The original book was a <i>Treatise on the Choir of the Blessed Virgin</i>, a book that dealt with theories about the kind of music that angels sing. The book was on the <i>Index Librorum Prohibitorum </i>of the Roman Catholic Church until 1966, when the Index was discontinued. The Grimoire that Katab found originally contained an &quot;appendix&quot; of rotes for cleansing fallen angels to restore them to their rightful place in the Choir, written by a scelestus who is currently being hunted by the Pentacle. But due to the grimoire being cast into the Ocean Oroboros by the Guardians, the appendix no longer works as intended (if it ever did), though it does have a strange effect on ghosts who read it. At the beginning of the chronicle the Mysterium caucus in Buenos Aires has made a request to the Sublime Athenaeum for any information regarding the original mundane book or corrupted grimoire copies, hinting that there may be a cult in Buenos Aires connected to the book </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm fine either way. Katab could be doing a favor for one of their ghost contacts (feel free to make one up on your own) or in the Ossuary with Davenant and the other Prospectors. Either way they get a message from Kintu about the request from Buenos Aires. I'm mainly looking for something that introduces your character in character and shows their perspective on death at the beginning of the chronicle.<br /> <br /> I was thinking the prologue scene would be in the IC thread (Think of the post I wrote as the opening scene of a show before the title sequence. A &quot;Cold Open&quot;. Then each PC gets an introduction scene) You can put the character introductions in the OOC thread like you and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a> did for &quot;In the Hallow Light&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T07:01:46-07:00","id":1517937,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28046-maroon_mumba\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar28046_1.webp');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28046\" data-vbnamecard=\"28046\">Maroon_Mumba</a> I was thinking your prologue scene could either be Blackfish meeting with Isla and Rigyom on Isla's ancestor island (&quot;Bone Garden&quot;), and deciding to go find Katab and other mages. Or if you want to cut to the chase, you could do a scene on board the Rachael with the ghost krewe on the way to Buenos Aires (about 4000 kilometers from Tristan)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T13:59:38-07:00","id":1517977,"title":"","content":"I think it more fun if we started with Isla meeting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28046-maroon_mumba","name":"Maroon_Mumba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28046_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T14:26:59-07:00","id":1517979,"title":"","content":"Cool! Put something in the IC and I'll respond.<br /> <br /> To mundane sight the island appears to be a very small island, less than an acre. Its not swimmable to access, even for a strong swimmer in human form. <br /> <br /> Or I suppose you could wait for her to come back from her father's <i>true</i> burial. Up to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-17T12:07:46-07:00","id":1518191,"title":"","content":"The first scene with all of the player characters is going to take place in Buenos Aires. I was thinking it would be interesting to have a short introduction to each character from their own perspective in the IC thread. But if you all would rather proceed directly to the opening group scene that is fine too.<br /> <br /> A brief Out of Character introduction to your character's info (Name, physical description, basic game stats) and background can go in the OOC thread.<br /> <br /> Sorry if what I said before was confusing. There is a learning curve to being a Story Teller in a Play-by-post as well as role playing in PbP. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-17T12:39:42-07:00","id":1518193,"title":"","content":"Buenos Aires has three consilia and a Free Council Assembly. The southern part of the city is the older part of the city and has many important government buildings. It's consilium has a Silver Ladder hierarch but is more dominated by the Arrow. The northern part of the city has the FC Assembly and a small consillum dominated by Silver Ladder Chinese immigrants and other immigrants from East Asia that is allied with the the south city consilium. There is a Pentacle consilium in the western city and suburbs. They tend to ally with the FC Assembly. There is also a significant Seer presence in the suburbs and the city of Rosario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-17T18:20:34-07:00","id":1518209,"title":"","content":"<b>Gilad</b><br /> <b>Name: </b>Erik Andersen<br /> <b>Age: </b>21<br /> <b>Height: </b>1.90m<br /> <b>Hair: </b>Blonde<br /> <b>Eyes: </b>Green<br /> <b>Path: </b>Thyrsus<br /> <b>Legacy (eventually): </b><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1391126-the-bannerets-of-ameretat-a-thyrsus-legacy-of-deathless-warriors\">Bannerets of Ameretat</a><br /> <b>Immediate Nimbus: </b>The echo of a martial music, which feels profoundly ancient, bolstering one's morale (+1 Resolve).<br /> <b>Signature Nimbus: </b>The deep breath before the plunge, the feeling of the approaching eve of battle.<br /> <b>Long Term Nimbus: </b>People tend to focus more on long term goals and are resolute in achieving them.<br /> <b>Dedicated Magical Tool: </b>A Spil\u00e5pipa with Swedish traditional wood carvings spelling the High Speech rune for &quot;Vigilance&quot;.<br /> <b>Concept: </b>The Eternal Warrior<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Background</b><br /> <br /> Erik Andersen was born in the island of \u00d6land, in the year 773 CE to a family of musicians. Both parents were court musicians, with his father keeping the lore of the Swedish traditions and his mother the Finnish ones.<br /> <br /> Following in his father\u2019s footsteps, he was trained in traditional music as well, being taught to draw inspiration from the sounds of the land. When warriors would return from great battles or from journeys to the edges of the world, it was his job to ensure their deeds would not be forgotten.<br /> <br /> His only other sibling, his older sister Alruna, was a skilled singer like their mother. She was known in the village and the Forts as a fortune teller. Women would often forbid her to come anywhere near a house with a pregnancy, even to the point of spitting on her and throwing stones. She carried small bones, possibly from a sea bird, with her and a clay bowl that she found buried somewhere with invisible writing that only she could read. She would sometimes disappear for days at a time without telling anyone where she was going. Sometimes Erik would see her playing in tidal pools and when he would ask her what she was doing she would laugh hysterically as if she was going mad.<br /> <br /> The last time Erik saw her, the wind was blowing fiercely from the sea, wiping her tunic and long unbraided hair around. It seemed as if the wind was going to blow the whole island away and things seemed to become un-solid as if he could see through them. He could hear her say, \u201cThere was a strong man with forty sons. Their mothers suffered ,except the last one. The men of the good island know this strong man. Their land is slowly drowning. One day these sons sailed far away to a place with good wind on a silver river.\u201d Then she started to cry and fell to her knees sobbing. She screamed \u201cDon\u2019t trust the virgin. Her eyes are too big, but she only sees far enough. She has a black pipe. Her song is beautiful, but her knives cut deep. There is another way\u2026\u201d and then she disappeared as if the wind blew her away like sea foam. Despite the family searching for weeks, they never found a trace of her.<br /> <br /> <b>The Awakening</b><br /> <br /> In the year of his 20th winter, on the 23rd of December, Erik undertook the final tradition to anoint him as a inheritor of his family's tradition, the \u00c5rsg\u00e5ng (Year Walk). Leaving his house in the dead of night, avoiding looking at any fires and not carrying provisions, he made his way to the forest of Trollskogen in search of insights from beyond.<br /> <br /> With only the moonlight to show him the path, he followed the tradition and walked deeper into the forest, until he reached an area where the caw of a rooster would never reach him. Walking through the moonlit forest, he noticed the surrounding fading, growing less corporeal, but the soul of the land and its people more vivid. The spirits seemed to be moving towards a mysterious, discordant song in the distance.<br /> <br /> Following them through the woods, Erik arrived at the shore overlooking the island of Bl\u00e5 Jungfrun, which the ancient tales warned about, the home of a coven practicing the most foul magic. Before he could notice, a deer in the form of a human stood before him. He claimed the music of the land was out of harmony, and that it would soon forget itself. He warned that it must remember its history in order to find the way forward. Almost as if responding to this being, a glowing cerulean river rose up from the sea, forming a path to the island. Erik, working on pure instinct, walked atop the river towards the dreaded shore.<br /> <br /> When he stepped onto the island, the discordant music sounded clearer than ever. He followed it through the woods and deep into the mountains, descending through a cave into the veins of the earth. In the depths lay an altar of stone and bone, overlooked by a Nachtkrapp, its coal red eyes fixed on the altar, its attention focused on playing a haunting melody using the holes in its wings. In the shadow of the torchlight, instruments made of bone were being played by the desiccated spirit of the departed.<br /> <br /> In his mind, Erik could hear the sound of the land, its pulse and rhythm like a heartbeat. Its melody was opposing the beast\u2019s. Before he could notice, he had taken his ax in hand and was fighting the monster to the beat of the music. Rhythmic parries and flank attacks slowly carved at the beast\u2019s hide, the fury of the dead becoming his armor.<br /> <br /> When the beast finally fell and he cast its ruin before him, the silence was broken by the sound of applause from a cloaked warrior. He mentioned that he had taken a chance, setting up this trial to find someone who can join their fight against an enemy from beyond, so he sought Alruna\u2019s brother. Before he could elaborate, reality seemed to flood, pushing them away in a fierce current, which washed reality away.<br /> <br /> By the time he could regain his footing, he was in a place of impossible architecture, where everything seemed to have a pastel look. The body of the Nachtkrapp was at his feet and the song of the land still rang in his ear. Looking at the holed wings of the creature, he started to carve the bones into a spil\u00e5pipa while humming the song.<br /> <br /> By the time he had finished, the deer humanoid was in front of him, this time wearing an odd outfit and carrying a glass of the cerulean liquid.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"333\" height=\"512\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://pm1.aminoapps.com/7928/b8c2bdbc7da02ba293fa085be2a187c4865f1fc1r1-570-874v2_00.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://pm1.aminoapps.com/7928/b8c2bdbc7da02ba293fa085be2a187c4865f1fc1r1-570-874v2_00.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://pm1.aminoapps.com/7928/b8c2bdbc7da02ba293fa085be2a187c4865f1fc1r1-570-874v2_00.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> Giving his blessing to the instrument, he poured the liquid into it, the bone transforming into birch wood, the water carving runes into the instrument. Erik proceeded to play the song on the spil\u00e5pipa, the surroundings melted away once more and he arrived back in \u00d6land in the present day. After joining the Arrow, he was placed in a traveling music band called Utopia, which acts as a cover to deploy operatives across the world. With traces of his former civilization lost to the sands of time, Erik hopes that somewhere in the world he will be able to find clues to the events surrounding his Awakening and Alruna\u2019s battle.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T16:12:13-07:00","id":1518274,"title":"","content":"First post in IC got flagged. Sorry for the delay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T19:11:53-07:00","id":1518286,"title":"","content":"No worries. Great description of the museum. Cool place for a gate!<br /> <br /> Clarification. Is this the meeting where Katab first aquired the item previously discussed, or is this the scene where they are summoned to Buenos Aires?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T19:50:18-07:00","id":1518289,"title":"","content":"The Buenos Aires summons. Their phone should go off soonish, which will surprise them because there shouldn\u2019t be signal in the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T07:46:15-07:00","id":1518309,"title":"","content":"Great!<br /> <br /> So it will be a call from Davenant, who looks and sounds somewhat like the actor Daniel Kaluuya. He says that the deal in Sydney will have to wait. Katab is urgently needed in Buenos Aires, for the reasons described in the previous spoiler post.<br /> <br /> There are two stops on a flight from Sydney to Buenos Aires. One in San Francisco, and another in Houston, TX. Stopping over in San Francisco might be a good opportunity to meet up with Gawain ( <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28057-nickeldan\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28057\" data-vbnamecard=\"28057\">nickeldan</a> 's character). We could say that he will serve as your temporary banner warden because of his experience in combatting Scelesti and Abyssal Entities.<br /> <br /> Do you want me to RP a response from Brady (and a reason for being in Sydney) or do you want to leave that open for now?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T07:53:17-07:00","id":1518310,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28057-nickeldan\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28057\" data-vbnamecard=\"28057\">nickeldan</a>, where you wanting to put a prologue scene for Gawain in the IC thread before meeting up with Katab in SF?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T08:06:34-07:00","id":1518311,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a>. Speaking of flight times. It looks like the most common stops on a flight from Oslo to Buenos Aires are in Amsterdam or Paris.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28046-maroon_mumba\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar28046_1.webp');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28046\" data-vbnamecard=\"28046\">Maroon_Mumba</a> is planning on going by <a href=\"https://www.cbc.ca/kids/images/ghost_ships_flying_dutchman.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">boat</a>, so we will say that Blackfish left earlier than the rest of you to arrive at roughly the same time. <br /> <br /> Everyone is certainly racking up the miles already! Remember that you take a beat every time you change from one city or region to another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T08:38:11-07:00","id":1518312,"title":"","content":"So potential scenes queued in the IC thread:<br /> <br /> Resolution of Sydney scene between Katab and ghost contact ( <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26736_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26736\" data-vbnamecard=\"26736\">TempleBuilder</a> and ST)<br /> Conversation between Blackfish and Isla ( <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28046-maroon_mumba\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar28046_1.webp');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28046\" data-vbnamecard=\"28046\">Maroon_Mumba</a> and ST)<br /> Prologue for Gawain ( <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28057-nickeldan\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28057\" data-vbnamecard=\"28057\">nickeldan</a> )<br /> Prologue for Gilad ( <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a> )<br /> Meeting between Katab and Gawain in San Francisco ( <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26736_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26736\" data-vbnamecard=\"26736\">TempleBuilder</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28057-nickeldan\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28057\" data-vbnamecard=\"28057\">nickeldan</a> )<br /> <br /> I think these would all be interesting scenes to RP. But if you all would rather fast forward to plot hooks in Buenos Aires that is fine too. <br /> <br /> I am fine with a player starting a scene of their own initiative if there is a clear story motivation, and I will respond to whatever you come up with. But if you would prefer for me to set up a scene and then have your character come in, that is fine too. Just let me know.<br /> <br /> The purpose of the OOC thread is to facilitate communication between players and storyteller that would normally occur around the table in a in-person game. The IC thread is for things that your character experiences within their own perspective. (Again. I think Cauthon, Temple, and Kaiser did a great job of this in the &quot;In the Hallowed Light&quot; chronicle threads).<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> <br /> OCC: I want my character to research that book in the library<br /> <br /> IC: At around midnight, [Character Name] rubs their eyes. <i>Will I ever find this clue</i>? They wondered.<br /> <br /> Also, remember that postings might not be instantaneous... because of Real Life. (I need that reminder too!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T15:09:37-07:00","id":1518326,"title":"","content":"A very cool way to find the old curator, scavaging historical curious that fall into the Great Below.<br /> <br /> I think it might be interesting for Gilad to start in Paris, since it would be a popular stop for Utopia. I was thinking someone wanted him to check rumors of a Place that Isn't, a haunted street that seems to be made of an architectonic colage of various cultures. Why is there a Place that Isn't in Death Twilight ? No idea, but one of the ghosts in there speaks Swedish, might as well see what they have to say.<br /> <br /> I need to add Destiny to his character sheet and remove the dot in Familiar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T13:38:47-07:00","id":1518373,"title":"","content":"Sure. So you could meet a metropolitan who is curious about the &quot;place that isn't&quot;. He is from Lebanon and his shadow name is Arjuani. In exchange for help with this mystery, he is willing to give you access to one of Paris' Athenaei to conduct research on Alruna's prophecy. The Swedish ghost is a an older ghost, a spy and diplomate who was in Paris, but was killed when France went to war with Sweden in 1805. The mystery of the place seems to have allowed him and several other ghosts to anchor themselves there rather than being swept into the underworld. They are all foreigners who would not normally stay in a strange city for long.<br /> <br /> Did you want to include any of the Utopia NPC or Trish in the scene?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T13:46:40-07:00","id":1518375,"title":"","content":"Meanwhile I am thinking that Caliburn and Nadeshiko have invited Gawain over to their farm. The family dog has died and the children wanted &quot;Uncle Ricky&quot; to come. While Caliburn and Gawain are digging the hole, Caliburn tells Gawain about the plan for him to go with Katab to Buenos Aires. Gawain also has an interest in Argentina because of some rumors about odd legends that have developed in Welsh immigrant community in Patagonia that relate to his academic research, and if it is on the Arrows dime than why not?<br /> <br /> Does that give you ( <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28057-nickeldan\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28057\" data-vbnamecard=\"28057\">nickeldan</a> ) enough to work with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T14:34:52-07:00","id":1518382,"title":"","content":"I think Harju, since between a Thyrsus and Obrimos, there is a decent Arcana spread. Plus he knows a good amount of languages, so we should be able to figure out a few things.<br /> <br /> Just to confirm, because of the original game's file for Trish, in this chronicle she is a Sleepwalker with a notion about the Orders and the secret world, correct ? So we don't have any restrictions on what she can see ? Because if so, she might be interested in seeing what this haunting is all about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T17:45:08-07:00","id":1518394,"title":"","content":"Trish has non-supernal supernatural powers so she is not quiescent but she does not posses mage sight or the ability to enter twilight on her own. Of the NPC that you are currently affiliated with, she is the best investigator, so she would be a good person to help with research. And if her luck were to rub off on you...<br /> <br /> I recently watched the Amazon Prime documentary series <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/gp/video/detail/B07N6M11C9/ref=atv_dp_share_cu_r\" target=\"_blank\">Hellier</a>. I feel like that would be the typical response of an unaffiliated sleepwalker/minor supernatural to a Mage mystery (it would also make a great basis for a mortals chronicle)<br /> <br /> <br /> Have you seen any 2E conversions for nWOD Second Sight templates (psychic/ thaumaturge)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T18:03:43-07:00","id":1518395,"title":"","content":"Neither does Gilad, entering Twilight is still an Arcana dot away, but <i>Touch of the Grave</i> will probably allow him to make do.<br /> <br /> I have yet to see the conversions, are they official or Storyteller's Vault ? What is the name of the book please ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T12:24:54-07:00","id":1518441,"title":"","content":"Oh. There actually is one in Storytellers Vault. Good thinking! <br /> <br /> Second Sight was a 1E book about non-Mage magic powers, similar to the supernatural templates in Hurt Locker. Dana Newkirk in Hellier would be a good example of a thaumaturge or low magic user. And Connor would be a good example of a psychic.<br /> <br /> I'm going to say that Trish has actually been on an assignment in Istanbul (Not Constantinople!), and meets Utopia in Paris. Lucas sends Gilad to pick her up at the Gare de l'Est train station, explaining that while Utopia does not normally want publicity, that working with this journalist might actually be helpful for the upcoming tour in South America. While he and she are there, they notice some odd things about the station building and get a little lost on their way back to the hotel.<br /> <br /> If you are wanting to roll play a little scene, actually, roll Wits+Persuasion, Wits+Stealth, and Death Unveiling and tell me what you get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T17:42:19-07:00","id":1518467,"title":"","content":"I think we can end Katab's bit there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T20:40:29-07:00","id":1518478,"title":"","content":"Sure. Brady will still be there if you should ever visit Sydney again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T12:41:32-07:00","id":1518657,"title":"","content":"Roger that:<br /> <br /> <i>Wits (2) + Persuasion (4):</i> <b>10</b>, <b>10</b>, <b>8</b>, 5, 3, 3, <b>9</b>, 2 -&gt; 4 successes<br /> <i>Wits (2) + Stealth (0):</i> 6, 4 -&gt; fail<br /> <i>Gnosis (1) + Death (2):</i><br /> 6, 4, 4 -&gt; fail<br /> <b>9</b>, 6, 2 -&gt; 1 success<br /> <br /> Sounds about right, Gilad didn't have stealth training, so his usual approach would be to walk into a place while giving off the impression of &quot;yes, I'm supposed to be here&quot;.<br /> <br /> Didn't know if he would have enough time to try the Death Unveiling again, so I made a second roll, just in case. In hindsight, I should have used willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-23-2023, 04:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T17:02:29-07:00","id":1518667,"title":"","content":"No worries. That's fine. I will say with four success you gain a perfect first impression with Trish for the purposes of social maneuvering. So roll play that as you will.<br /> <br /> You notice as Trish is getting off the train that she is being followed by the ghost of a little girl who is dressed in 1940s era clothes.<br /> <br /> And you don't notice anything else. \ud83d\ude09","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T17:03:39-07:00","id":1518668,"title":"","content":"I'm going to do a little scene with Gawain and then we can do Paris. I think that has the best story flow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T05:50:20-07:00","id":1518924,"title":"","content":"Just checking in<br /> I think what we have in queue is:<br /> <br /> A scene between Gawain ( <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28057-nickeldan\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28057\" data-vbnamecard=\"28057\">nickeldan</a> ) and his mentor<br /> Gilad and Trish in Paris<br /> Blackfish and Isla on her island<br /> <br /> And then I think everyone will be in Buenos Aires together ready to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T21:03:20-07:00","id":1518989,"title":"","content":"OOC:<br /> <br /> Name: Richard Humphrey<br /> Shadow name: Gawain<br /> Age: 25<br /> Path: Obrimos<br /> Order: Adamantine Arrow<br /> Dedicated magical tool: English broadsword<br /> <br /> Rich Humphrey is the third son of a wealthy family from the LA area. With one of his older brothers running for Congress and the other on track to take over the family's law firm, Rich is mostly overlooked by his parents. So, when he expressed a fascination with medieval literature, they shrugged and called in some favors at UC Berkeley.<br /> <br /> During his Junior year, while working on his term paper on Sir Gawain and the Green Knight, he began to see the Reality behind the tale. All of human history centered on the victory and establishment of human order and reason (Camelot) over the chaos of this world (the Green Knight). After managing to cram his lofty revelation into human words, he went to turn in his paper. Luckily, the professor reminded him to write his name on it. As Rich turned to walk to his next class, the professor advised him to &quot;Prepare.&quot;<br /> <br /> While possessing a mediocre physique, his passion and drive caught the eye of Caliburn of the Adamantine Arrow. Over the next four years, Gawain (as he decided to call himself) was transformed into an accomplished swordsman.<br /> \u200b<br /> IC:<br /> <br /> The sun was low by the time the grave digger put in the last shovel of dirt. The youngest of the mourners let out a small whimper and clung to her mother's skirts. Gawain put down his shovel and wiped his hands on his trousers. He was not kin to the deceased and merely being invited to the ceremony was a tremendous honor. Digging the grave was the least he could do.<br /> <br /> The family patriarch stood next to him. &quot;Richard,&quot; he began with a quiet voice full of emotion. &quot;Would you care to say a few words?&quot;<br /> <br /> Gawain, or Richard as he was known to the uninitiated, swallowed nervously. This was unexpected but, in retrospect, shouldn't have been. Everything was a test under his master's tutelage. He nodded and stepped forward.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ares was a noble friend like none other. He was a gentle soul and yet a fearless warrior when needed be. We are grateful for the life he shared with us. We remember all that he was and celebrate the part of him he leaves with us. You shall be missed, old man.&quot;<br /> <br /> The matriarch walked over and put a hand on Gawain's shoulder. &quot;Thank you, dear. That was beautiful.&quot;<br /> <br /> Later that night, after the kids had been put to bed, Gawain and his master sat on the front porch nursing their beers. &quot;Thanks for coming,&quot; Caliburn said. &quot;The kids always love to see you. Real tear-jerker of a speech too though it's more than that flea-ridden old mutt deserved.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Don't speak ill of the dead,&quot; Gawain replied with a grin.<br /> <br /> A moment passed. Caliburn took a swig of his bear and sighed. &quot;So, down to business. Your passport up to date?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28057-nickeldan","name":"nickeldan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T04:44:13-07:00","id":1519002,"title":"","content":"Great!<br /> <br /> Sorry I changed it from a dog to a cat in the IC thread. I remembered that Trish had a cat in Dave's game in London. Very helpful for combating &quot;spiders&quot;.<br /> <br /> I really like the diversity of characters we have here. West Coast grad student, Scrappy &quot;acquisitions expert&quot; from Boston, time traveling Viking, remote African island fisherman. And every one has a slightly different perspective on death.<br /> <br /> So next we'll catch up with Gilad and Trish in Paris. And then come full circle back to Blackfish.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T06:20:13-07:00","id":1519245,"title":"","content":"Sorry. The forum glitched my post. Hopefully what Caliburn said makes sense.<br /> <br /> Also, to be clear, I as the ST know that Gilad might not know French. Trish as a character is making an assumption. Do with that as you will.<br /> <br /> I'm going to say that Gilad takes on a &quot;Lost in Time&quot; condition. Every time he fails to recognize a social cue or some detail because of his unfamiliarity with his temporal surroundings (wits+composure or relevant skill) he can choose to take a beat, up to five per chapter. The condition resolves when he gains some understanding the modern world by successfully opening a social door or finding an investigation clue.<br /> <br /> I'm going to give Katab and Gawain the informed condition on their next investigative roll for dealing with the abyssal intrusion in Buenos Aires.<br /> <br /> Clues so far<br /> (For Katab) It has something to do with the book that he found a castoff of. &quot;The Angelic Choir of the Virgin&quot;.<br /> (For Gawain) Caliburn thinks it has something to do with Annunaki and seductive &quot;singing&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T19:01:00-07:00","id":1519307,"title":"","content":"Ah, ok. I was a bit confused because I thought we were tackling the scenarios in order, so I was waiting for Gawain's one to play out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}